<< /A 3558 0 R /ADBE_FT << /Initial 7 >> /Alt (Fig. 4: The figure presents bar charts comparing agreement scores of user-defined gestures for Animal Crossing: New Horizons and Kirby Star Allies. Core movement actions such as walking and running show high agreement in both games. In Animal Crossing, daily-life actions \(e.g., shaking trees, watering plants, catching fish, placing items\) show higher agreement, while spatial actions such as climbing cliffs show lower agreement. In Kirby, basic movement and thrust actions show higher agreement, whereas more abstract or ability-based actions \(e.g., opening chests, sword spins, ice slide\) show lower agreement.\000) /C /adbe_style_005001 /ID (AD260421-2200-1186-ADBE-000000012995) /K [ 2 82 81 80 79 78 77 76 84 83 85 97 96 95 94 93 92 91 90 89 88 87 86 115 114 113 112 111 110 109 108 107 106 105 104 103 102 101 100 99 98 ] /P 1262 0 R /Pg 319 0 R /S /Figure >>
endobj
